yield: per-serve
ingredients:
  - item: tequila blanco
    mass: 45
  - item: lime juice
    mass: 15
  - item: grapefruit soda
    mass: 120
    note: Ting or Jarritos; sub 60g fresh grapefruit juice + 60g soda water
  - item: salt
    note: pinch in the drink, plus a rim if you want it
steps:
  - salt the rim with a lime wedge if using
  - tequila and lime into a highball over ice
  - top with grapefruit soda, stir once gently to keep the fizz
notes: |
  Pairs with breakfast/sourdough-skillet — the sharp citrus cleanses the palate after the
  rich bacon and feta.

  Fresh grapefruit juice + soda is the better drink but needs the pinch of salt more; the
  soda version is already sweet enough to carry it.
